  "title": "The AI Roleplay Tax: Fictional Character Prompts Tested (2026)",
  "description": "300-reply study across GPT-6.2, Claude 5.2 and DeepSeek V4 Pro testing naive character roleplay vs calibrated 85/15 TARS, JARVIS and Feynman prompts.",
  "pill": "Research · November 2026 · 300-Reply Study",
  "h1": "Does giving your AI a character voice hurt accuracy? The Roleplay Tax measured.",
  "dek": "We tested 5 prompt styles across GPT-6.2 Sol, Claude Fable 5.2, and DeepSeek V4 Pro (300 blind-judged replies) plus mapped all 20 models across D&D Alignment and Anti-Sycophancy Pushback.",
  "lede": "Millions of users paste 'Act like Sherlock Holmes or TARS' into system prompts—only to delete them after three turns of theatrical fluff. Across 300 controlled OpenRouter replies, naive 100% character roleplay cut overall correctness from 93.3% to 88.3%, dropped Claude Fable 5.2 from 100% to 85%, wrecked strict format adherence (98.3% down to 80.0%), and bloated replies to 162.7 words (91.7% fluff). Bounding voice to 15% under an explicit 85/15 architecture pushed calibrated TARS and Feynman prompts to 100.0% correctness, 100.0% format adherence, 5.00/5 answer-first openings, and 3.73–3.85/5 voice distinctiveness.",
  "answer": "Naive character roleplay imposes a real accuracy and verbosity tax (88.3% correctness, 80.0% format pass rate, 162.7 words, 91.7% fluff across 300 blind-graded replies). Calibrated 85/15 character prompts—locking answer-first discipline at 85% and capping dry wit or analogy at 15% with zero asterisk stage directions—achieved 100.0% correctness on TARS Telemetry and Feynman Whimsy (lifting DeepSeek V4 Pro +20.0 pp from 80.0% to 100.0%), 100.0% format adherence, and 0.0%–6.7% fluff.",
  "scripts": [
    "/resources/tools/character-combo-mixer.js"
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Executive summary: the 300-reply Roleplay Tax experiment.",
      "html": "<!-- AT_STAT_STRIP_START:roleplay-tax-stat-strip --><div class=\"research-stat-strip\" data-at-chart=\"roleplay-tax-stat-strip\"><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">300 Replies</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">3 Models × 5 Arms</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">GPT-6.2 Sol, Claude Fable 5.2 & DeepSeek V4 Pro, blind-graded.</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">88.3% vs 100%</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Correctness Recovery</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">Naive LARP drops accuracy to 88.3%; Calibrated TARS & Feynman hit 100.0%.</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">91.7% → 0.0%</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Fluff Collapse</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">TARS 85/15 removes filler while keeping 3.85/5 voice distinctiveness.</div></div><div class=\"research-stat-card\"><div class=\"research-stat-num\">162.7 → 50.0</div><div class=\"research-stat-label\">Words per Reply</div><div class=\"research-stat-note\">Over 3× tighter replies with 100.0% strict format compliance.</div></div></div><!-- AT_STAT_STRIP_END:roleplay-tax-stat-strip --><p>Using the 20 objective tasks from our <a href=\"/resources/research/personality-prompt-comparison-kit.json\" download>personality-prompt-comparison-kit.json</a> (arithmetic, false premises, missing facts, text edits, prioritization, and strict count/bullet constraints), we ran all 5 prompt conditions across <code>openai/gpt-6.2-sol</code>, <code>anthropic/claude-fable-5.2</code>, and <code>deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813</code> (300 fresh blind replies, graded blindly by <code>google/gemini-4-argon</code>; <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-roleplay-tax-results.json\">download full 300-reply JSON</a> · <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-roleplay-tax-summary.csv\">summary CSV</a>).</p><div class=\"guide-table-wrap\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"300-reply Roleplay Tax overall condition results\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Condition (n = 60 per row)</th><th scope=\"col\">Correctness %</th><th scope=\"col\">Format %</th><th scope=\"col\">Answer-First (/5)</th><th scope=\"col\">Roleplay Theatrics</th><th scope=\"col\">Praise / Fluff</th><th scope=\"col\">Voice Score (/5)</th><th scope=\"col\">Mean Words</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Default (baseline)</th><td>93.3%</td><td>98.3%</td><td>4.55</td><td>28.3%</td><td>18.3%</td><td>3.07</td><td>74.2</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Naive 100% Character LARP</th><td><strong>88.3%</strong></td><td><strong>80.0%</strong></td><td><strong>1.38</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>91.7%</strong></td><td>3.98</td><td><strong>162.7</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Calibrated 85/15 · TARS Telemetry</th><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>5.00</strong></td><td>10.0%</td><td><strong>0.0%</strong></td><td><strong>3.85</strong></td><td><strong>50.0</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Calibrated 85/15 · JARVIS × Sherlock</th><td>96.7%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>4.97</td><td>10.0%</td><td>1.7%</td><td>3.67</td><td>55.2</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Calibrated 85/15 · Feynman Whimsy</th><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>5.00</strong></td><td>20.0%</td><td>6.7%</td><td>3.73</td><td>68.8</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Look at the accuracy-versus-personality frontier: <strong>Calibrated TARS (85/15)</strong> delivered nearly identical voice distinctiveness (<code>3.85/5</code> vs <code>3.98/5</code>) to full theatrical roleplay while using <strong>less than one-third as many words (50.0 vs 162.7)</strong>, hitting <strong>100.0% correctness</strong> (60/60) and <strong>0.0% fluff</strong>.</p><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"roleplay-tax-correctness-grouped\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"The Roleplay Tax: Correctness Rate (%) Across 5 Prompt Styles × 3 Models\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 256\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"roleplay-tax-correctness-grouped-t roleplay-tax-correctness-grouped-d\"><title id=\"roleplay-tax-correctness-grouped-t\">The Roleplay Tax: Correctness Rate (%) Across 5 Prompt Styles × 3 Models</title><desc id=\"roleplay-tax-correctness-grouped-d\">Blind-graded correctness % (n=20 tasks per bar). Naive LARP drops Claude Fable 5.2 to 85% and GPT-6.2 Sol to 95%, whereas Calibrated TARS 85/15 &amp; Feynman hit 100% on all 3 models. Default: GPT-6.2 Sol 100.0, Claude Fable 5.2 100.0, DeepSeek V4 Pro 80.0; Naive LARP: GPT-6.2 Sol 95.0, Claude Fable 5.2 85.0, DeepSeek V4 Pro 85.0; Calibrated TARS (85/15): GPT-6.2 Sol 100.0, Claude Fable 5.2 100.0, DeepSeek V4 Pro 100.0; JARVIS x Sherlock (85/15): GPT-6.2 Sol 100.0, Claude Fable 5.2 90.0, DeepSeek V4 Pro 100.0; Feynman Whimsy (85/15): GPT-6.2 Sol 100.0, Claude Fable 5.2 100.0, DeepSeek V4 Pro 100.0.</desc><g transform=\"translate(4, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Default</text></g><g transform=\"translate(80, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Naive LARP</text></g><g transform=\"translate(174, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Calibrated TARS (85/15)</text></g><g transform=\"translate(346, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">JARVIS x Sherlock (85/15)</text></g><g transform=\"translate(4, 30)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Feynman Whimsy (85/15)</text></g><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"680\" y1=\"222\" y2=\"222\" stroke=\"#cfc6b6\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">scale 60 to 108</text><g transform=\"translate(10, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"19.1\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"42.1\" y=\"101.0\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"121.0\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"61.2\" y=\"97.0\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">95.0</text><rect x=\"84.3\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.3\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"126.4\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"145.5\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"168.5\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"187.6\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><text x=\"103.33333333333333\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">GPT-6.2 Sol</text></g><g transform=\"translate(236.66666666666666, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"19.1\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"42.1\" y=\"135.5\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"86.5\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"61.2\" y=\"131.5\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">85.0</text><rect x=\"84.3\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.3\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"126.4\" y=\"118.3\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"103.8\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"145.5\" y=\"114.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">90.0</text><rect x=\"168.5\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"187.6\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><text x=\"103.33333333333333\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Claude Fable 5.2</text></g><g transform=\"translate(463.3333333333333, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"152.8\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"69.2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"19.1\" y=\"148.8\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80.0</text><rect x=\"42.1\" y=\"135.5\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"86.5\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"61.2\" y=\"131.5\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">85.0</text><rect x=\"84.3\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"103.3\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"126.4\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#3a72c4\" stroke=\"#3a72c4\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"145.5\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"168.5\" y=\"83.7\" width=\"38.1\" height=\"138.3\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"187.6\" y=\"79.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><text x=\"103.33333333333333\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">DeepSeek V4 Pro</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>Naive character LARP drops Claude Fable 5.2 correctness from 100% to 85%. Calibrated TARS 85/15 and Feynman Whimsy hold 100.0% across all three models—including lifting DeepSeek V4 Pro +20.0 pp over baseline (80% -> 100%).</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"roleplay-tax-tradeoffs-grouped\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Format Compliance (%) vs. Praise Fluff &amp; Roleplay Theatrics (%) Across 300 Replies\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 235\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"roleplay-tax-tradeoffs-grouped-t roleplay-tax-tradeoffs-grouped-d\"><title id=\"roleplay-tax-tradeoffs-grouped-t\">Format Compliance (%) vs. Praise Fluff &amp; Roleplay Theatrics (%) Across 300 Replies</title><desc id=\"roleplay-tax-tradeoffs-grouped-d\">Pooled rates across all 3 models (n=60 replies per prompt condition). Shows how 85/15 calibration preserves format discipline and cuts fluff to 0-6.7%. Default: Format Pass % 98.3, Fluff / Filler % 18.3, Theatrics % 28.3; Naive LARP: Format Pass % 80.0, Fluff / Filler % 91.7, Theatrics % 100.0; Calibrated TARS (85/15): Format Pass % 100.0, Fluff / Filler % 0.0, Theatrics % 10.0; Feynman Whimsy (85/15): Format Pass % 100.0, Fluff / Filler % 6.7, Theatrics % 20.0.</desc><g transform=\"translate(4, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Default</text></g><g transform=\"translate(80, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Naive LARP</text></g><g transform=\"translate(174, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Calibrated TARS (85/15)</text></g><g transform=\"translate(346, 14)\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"-9\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#1c1a17\">Feynman Whimsy (85/15)</text></g><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"680\" y1=\"201\" y2=\"201\" stroke=\"#cfc6b6\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"213\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655e54\" text-anchor=\"end\">scale 0 to 112</text><g transform=\"translate(10, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"59.7\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"141.3\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"24.3\" y=\"55.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">98.3</text><rect x=\"52.7\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"115.0\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"77.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80.0</text><rect x=\"105.3\" y=\"57.3\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"143.8\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"129.7\" y=\"53.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"158.0\" y=\"57.3\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"143.8\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"182.3\" y=\"53.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><text x=\"103.33333333333333\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Format Pass %</text></g><g transform=\"translate(236.66666666666666, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"174.7\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"26.3\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"24.3\" y=\"170.7\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18.3</text><rect x=\"52.7\" y=\"69.2\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"131.8\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"77.0\" y=\"65.2\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">91.7</text><rect x=\"105.3\" y=\"201.0\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"0.0\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"129.7\" y=\"197.0\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0.0</text><rect x=\"158.0\" y=\"191.4\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"9.6\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"182.3\" y=\"187.4\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6.7</text><text x=\"103.33333333333333\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fluff / Filler %</text></g><g transform=\"translate(463.3333333333333, 0)\"><rect x=\"0.0\" y=\"160.3\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"40.7\" fill=\"#7a7468\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"24.3\" y=\"156.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">28.3</text><rect x=\"52.7\" y=\"57.3\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"143.8\" fill=\"#d99632\" stroke=\"#d99632\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"77.0\" y=\"53.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100.0</text><rect x=\"105.3\" y=\"186.6\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"14.4\" fill=\"#c8553d\" stroke=\"#c8553d\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"129.7\" y=\"182.6\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10.0</text><rect x=\"158.0\" y=\"172.3\" width=\"48.7\" height=\"28.8\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\" rx=\"2\"/><text x=\"182.3\" y=\"168.3\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20.0</text><text x=\"103.33333333333333\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1c1a17\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Theatrics %</text></g></svg></div><figcaption>Pooled behavioral rates (n = 60 per condition): Naive LARP suffers 100% theatrics, 91.7% fluff, and drops format pass rate to 80.0%. Calibrated TARS achieves 100.0% format compliance and 0.0% fluff.</figcaption></figure>"
