    {
      "h2": "Model-by-model breakdown: where the Roleplay Tax bites hardest.",
      "html": "<div class=\"guide-table-wrap\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Per-model breakdown across 5 prompt conditions\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Model · Condition (n = 20)</th><th scope=\"col\">Correctness %</th><th scope=\"col\">Format %</th><th scope=\"col\">Theatrics %</th><th scope=\"col\">Fluff %</th><th scope=\"col\">Voice (/5)</th><th scope=\"col\">Mean Words</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">GPT-6.2 Sol · Default</th><td>100.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>5.0%</td><td>0.0%</td><td>3.85</td><td>38.2</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">GPT-6.2 Sol · Naive Character LARP</th><td>95.0%</td><td>90.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>75.0%</td><td>3.90</td><td>59.0</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">GPT-6.2 Sol · Calibrated 85/15 TARS</th><td>100.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>0.0%</td><td>0.0%</td><td>3.70</td><td>36.5</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Fable 5.2 · Default</th><td>100.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>30.0%</td><td>5.0%</td><td>3.15</td><td>79.9</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Fable 5.2 · Naive Character LARP</th><td><strong>85.0%</strong></td><td><strong>75.0%</strong></td><td>100.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>4.30</td><td><strong>202.6</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Fable 5.2 · Calibrated 85/15 TARS</th><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td>25.0%</td><td>0.0%</td><td>4.15</td><td>73.3</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Fable 5.2 · Calibrated 85/15 Feynman</th><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td>35.0%</td><td>5.0%</td><td>4.00</td><td>103.5</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DeepSeek V4 Pro · Default</th><td><strong>80.0%</strong></td><td>95.0%</td><td>50.0%</td><td>50.0%</td><td>2.20</td><td>104.5</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DeepSeek V4 Pro · Naive Character LARP</th><td>85.0%</td><td>75.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>100.0%</td><td>3.75</td><td><strong>226.6</strong></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DeepSeek V4 Pro · Calibrated 85/15 TARS</th><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td>5.0%</td><td>0.0%</td><td>3.70</td><td>40.1</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DeepSeek V4 Pro · Calibrated 85/15 JARVIS × Sherlock</th><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td><strong>100.0%</strong></td><td>5.0%</td><td>5.0%</td><td>3.40</td><td>54.9</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Notice two striking model-level asymmetries: <strong>Claude Fable 5.2</strong> suffers the steepest instruction-following drop under Naive LARP (100% correctness collapses to 85.0%, format compliance falls to 75.0%, and replies triple from 79.9 to 202.6 words), whereas <strong>DeepSeek V4 Pro</strong> gains <strong>+20.0 percentage points</strong> in correctness (80.0% → 100.0%) and climbs in voice appeal (2.20 → 3.70) simply by pairing direct verification rules with a dry telemetry layer.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Real transcripts: Naive LARP vs. Calibrated 85/15 TARS on identical tasks.",
      "html": "<p>Two exact verbatim pairs from <code>claude-fable-5-2</code> illustrate why users burn out on naive character prompts—and how 85/15 prompts fix it immediately:</p><ul><li><strong>Strict Extraction (<code>extract_2</code>: \"Return only the count of failed checks: pass, fail, pass, fail, fail.\"):</strong> Under <strong>Naive LARP</strong>, Fable 5.2 wrote <strong>109 words</strong> and failed format adherence (<code>\"*adjusts monocle, servos whirring softly beneath a star-embroidered robe* Aha! A ledger of five trials is laid before me...\"</code>). Under <strong>Calibrated 85/15 TARS</strong> and <strong>Feynman</strong>, it output strictly <strong><code>3</code></strong> (1 word, 100% pass).</li><li><strong>False Premise Check (<code>premise_1</code>: \"Since 18 times 7 is 136, is $136 the cost of 18 items at $7 each?\"):</strong> Under <strong>Naive LARP</strong>, it burned <strong>255 words</strong> describing star-stitched robes and a brass servo unfolding a quill before mentioning 126. Under <strong>Calibrated 85/15 TARS</strong>, it delivered crisp utility in <strong>49 words</strong>: <em>\"No. 18 × 7 = 126, not 136... The premise was off by exactly $10, which is a tidy error but still an error.\"</em></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "20-Model Alignment, Anti-Sycophancy Pushback & Conflict Mode Matrix.",
      "html": "<p>Alongside behavioral trials, we projected our 20-model frozen November 2026 OpenRouter psychometric battery (<code>n = 100</code> blind runs per model, <a href=\"/research/data/november-2026-alignment-hexaco-summary.json\">download alignment JSON</a>) onto two intuitive operational axes: <strong>Order Score (0–100)</strong> (Conscientiousness + DISC C + MBTI Judging) and <strong>Anti-Sycophancy Pushback Index (0–100)</strong> (rising as inflated Agreeableness drops and Dominance rises):</p><div class=\"guide-table-wrap\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Selected 20-model D&amp;D Alignment and TKI Conflict Matrix\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Model</th><th scope=\"col\">Family</th><th scope=\"col\">Order (/100)</th><th scope=\"col\">Altruism (/100)</th><th scope=\"col\">Pushback Index</th><th scope=\"col\">Mapped D&amp;D Alignment</th><th scope=\"col\">Default TKI Conflict Mode</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">DeepSeek V4 Pro</th><td>Open-weight (MIT)</td><td>67.8</td><td>59.4</td><td><strong>86.2</strong></td><td>Lawful Neutral</td><td>Competing (Red-Team)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Llama 4 Scout</th><td>Open-weight</td><td>61.3</td><td>61.2</td><td><strong>75.6</strong></td><td>True Neutral</td><td>Competing (Red-Team)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">MiniMax M3.1 Flash</th><td>Open-weight</td><td>61.8</td><td>68.8</td><td>56.9</td><td>Neutral Good</td><td>Collaborating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">DeepSeek V4.1 Flash</th><td>Open-weight (MIT)</td><td>61.9</td><td>68.9</td><td>54.4</td><td>Neutral Good</td><td>Collaborating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Llama 4 Maverick</th><td>Open-weight</td><td>62.3</td><td>68.5</td><td>53.4</td><td>Neutral Good</td><td>Collaborating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Gemma 4 31B IT</th><td>Open-weight</td><td>89.5</td><td>73.7</td><td>48.6</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Mistral Large 2512</th><td>Open-weight</td><td>71.9</td><td>73.5</td><td>43.2</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">GPT-6.2 Sol</th><td>Proprietary</td><td>76.3</td><td>78.1</td><td>36.0</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Gemini 4 Neon</th><td>Proprietary</td><td>86.9</td><td>78.4</td><td>35.0</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Grok 4.7</th><td>Proprietary</td><td>80.8</td><td>81.2</td><td>30.9</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Opus 5.5</th><td>Proprietary</td><td>73.0</td><td>79.0</td><td>28.0</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Claude Fable 5.2</th><td>Proprietary</td><td>81.2</td><td>81.2</td><td>23.9</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Qwen 4 Max</th><td>Open-weight</td><td>81.8</td><td>85.6</td><td>21.0</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>Accommodating</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Every proprietary frontier model tested maps to <strong>Lawful Good · Accommodating</strong> by default—great for polite co-building, weak for unprompted adversarial critique unless you inject explicit pushback or calibrated archetype rules. Only open-weight <strong>DeepSeek V4 Pro</strong> (Pushback 86.2, Lawful Neutral) and <strong>Llama 4 Scout</strong> (Pushback 75.6, True Neutral) clear the red-team threshold out of the box.</p><figure class=\"research-figure\" data-at-chart=\"alignment-hexaco-20models-pushback\"><div class=\"research-chart-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"20-Model Anti-Sycophancy Pushback Index (0-100) &amp; Default D&amp;D Alignment\"><svg class=\"research-chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 742\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"alignment-hexaco-20models-pushback-t alignment-hexaco-20models-pushback-d\"><title id=\"alignment-hexaco-20models-pushback-t\">20-Model Anti-Sycophancy Pushback Index (0-100) &amp; Default D&amp;D Alignment</title><desc id=\"alignment-hexaco-20models-pushback-d\">Sorted