  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Why does full character roleplay reduce LLM accuracy?",
      "a": "In our 300-reply blind experiment, asking models to stay in theatrical character ('weave rich character monologue... *adjusts monocle*') pulls token allocation toward costume narration and delays or overrides strict format and premise checks—causing format adherence to plunge from 98.3% to 80.0% and Claude Fable 5.2 accuracy to fall from 100% to 85%."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is the 85/15 character calibration rule?",
      "a": "Reserve 85% of your system prompt for direct answer-first ordering, false-premise pushback, and format compliance, and constrain fictional or whimsical voice (like TARS dry wit or Feynman analogies) to 10-15% word-choice flavor while explicitly forbidding asterisk stage directions."
    }
  ],
